# Wayland flags for apps under bspwm-wl (from Omarchy x-wing ~/.config/*-flags.conf).
# Reference only: nothing reads this automatically yet, so the X11 bspwm
# launchers are not affected. To use, append to the app's launcher command.
#
# brave / chromium / chrome:
#   --ozone-platform=wayland --ozone-platform-hint=wayland
#   --enable-features=TouchpadOverscrollHistoryNavigation
#   --password-store=gnome-libsecret
#   (Omarchy also adds --disable-features=WaylandWpColorManagerV1, a Hyprland-only crash workaround,
#    and --load-extension=/usr/share/omarchy/... paths that do not exist here: omitted)
# electron apps (electron-flags.conf):
#   --enable-features=UseOzonePlatform --ozone-platform=wayland
#   or env: ELECTRON_OZONE_PLATFORM_HINT=wayland
#   NOT applied to the Grok Bot app (it runs fine via XWayland; changing it risks the connection).
